Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: cd321x: drain queued updates on probe unwind

Initial connect may queue update_work before IRQ registration. If that
registration fails, stop the update before freeing the partner and
port resources. Also drain updates in CD321x unregister for other
probe-error paths. The cancel operation is idempotent on the normal
remove path.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
@@ -1328,6 +1328,9 @@
 {
 	struct cd321x *cd321x = container_of(tps, struct cd321x, tps);
 
+	/* Probe unwind can reach here after connect() queued an update. */
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&cd321x->update_work);
+
 	typec_thunderbolt_switch_put(cd321x->tbt_switch);
 	cd321x->tbt_switch = NULL;
 	typec_mux_put(cd321x->mux);
@@ -1862,6 +1865,9 @@
 	return 0;
 
 err_disconnect:
+	/* Stop asynchronous partner updates before disconnect frees the partner. */
+	if (tps->data->remove)
+		tps->data->remove(tps);
 	tps6598x_disconnect(tps, 0);
 err_unregister_port:
 	tps->data->unregister_port(tps);
